title: MackenzieJoyceClue0
---
On a cloudy afternoon, a teenage Mackenzie was on a walk with her dog. A small beagle mix, Charlie pulled tight at the leash. Mackenzie notice that the trail she walked nearly every day was a lot less busy than usual. There was an unnerving quiet. All of a sudden, tornado sirens erupted out of the silence. Right below one of the sirens, Mackenzie collapsed to the ground, covering her ears. It shook her bones. Charlie whimpered at her feet. Mackenzie just sat there in a ball, rocking back and forth. She eventually worked up the nerve to wrap her jacket around her head and fight her way back home. 
===

title: MackenzieJoyceClue1
---
At a sleepway camp when Mackenzie was fifteen, she awoke suddenly in the middle of the night. Everything looked strange, like she was wearing red-tinted glasses. She looked down to see her shirt soaked in blood. She screamed and grabbed at her face. She was bleeding out of her eyes, ears, and nose. The noise woke her roommate up, who promptly called the camp counselor over. She was in and out of consciousness, until she awoke in a hospital bed. She apparently had a terrible nose bleed while sleeping that caused blood to fill her sinuses. She returned to camp, but feared falling asleep every night. 
===

title: MackenzieJoyceClue2
---
On her eighteenth birthday, Mackenzie had gone out early to walk her dog. Her family had a whole day planned out and she wanted to have some time to herself before the craziness began. While walking on a poorly maintained part of the trail, Charlie stopped and stared at a shaking bush fencing off the mangled brush from the rest of the path. Suddenly, a snarling black dog came tumbling out of the brush, foaming at the mouth. The dog lunged at Charlie. Mackenzie screamed at the top of her lungs, but there was no one around. The attacker had Charlie’s abdomen firmly in its mouth and flung the small dog back and forth. The last bit of air to leave Charlie’s lung created a sharp bark that reverberated through the trees. The last thing Mackznie saw before fleeing was the old beagle’s body covered in saliva and blood. 
===